SEARCH = "https://vishnuprasad.space/work/enterprise-search"
E("enterprise-search", "Intelligent Enterprise Search Platform",
  ["enterprise search", "intelligent search", "search platform", "unify search", "unifyapps search",
   "knowledge search", "search product", "search case study", "ai search", "search engine", "copilot search",
   "agent marketplace", "connectors", "connector management", "search"],
  overview="**Intelligent Enterprise Search Platform (UnifyApps)**\n\nAn AI-powered search platform that connects all of a company's tools into one shared knowledge index, so people get **direct answers with sources** instead of searching system after system.\n\n- **Role:** Lead Product Designer, end to end from client brief to developer handoff\n- **Platform:** Web and mobile\n- **Timeline:** 2025 – present\n- **Core idea:** in enterprise AI, trust is the product" + L(SEARCH),
  problem="Organisations had the information they needed, but it was scattered across documents, chat tools and business apps. Five problems stood out:\n\n1. Search returned **files, not answers**\n2. Knowledge sat in **disconnected systems** with no single place to manage it\n3. Results **ignored who was asking** and their role\n4. Teams **couldn't customise** the experience without engineering\n5. Users **couldn't see how their data was handled**, which hurt trust",
  users="The platform serves three roles, each with a different need:\n\n- **Employees** want clear, trustworthy answers with sources\n- **Administrators** want to manage integrations, permissions and settings without engineering help\n- **Compliance teams** want to see what data the platform can access, how it's used, and audit it\n\nThe product team defined these roles and led the research; their findings shaped every design decision.",
  features="Five core capabilities, each solving one of the five problems:\n\n- **Connect Applications:** Slack, Jira, GitHub, Google Drive and more in one knowledge base, with clear connection statuses\n- **Manage Connections:** admins see what's syncing, choose what's included and see failures\n- **Personalised Results:** direct, role-aware answers with sources instead of file lists\n- **Customise Enterprise Search:** branding, wording, enabled tools and AI model through plain-language settings\n- **Agent Marketplace:** ready-made agents for finance, legal, sales and operations, each showing what it does and whether it's verified",
  strategy="Vishnu designed the platform as a **copilot**: Search, Chat, Agents, Spaces and Apps share one index and one interaction model.\n\nResponsibility grows across three levels:\n\n1. **Ask:** employees get answers\n2. **Configure:** admins shape the experience\n3. **Govern:** compliance oversees access and use\n\nThis lets one product serve everyone without each role seeing complexity it doesn't need.",
  decisions="Key decisions:\n\n- **A marketplace instead of only an agent builder:** most people want to use good agents, not build them, and successful agents get reused across the company\n- **Failures shown openly:** sync failures and unverified agents are visible, because hiding them would erode trust\n- **Plain-language admin settings:** admins configure AI behaviour without engineering, at the cost of fewer low-level controls in that view",
  outcomes="These are **UnifyApps' published figures** from a large financial institution's deployment; Vishnu did not measure them himself:\n\n- ~**$5.5M** projected annual cost savings\n- **800K+** consents captured in the first two weeks\n- **90% faster** time-to-market (two weeks vs. a typical 12–18 months)\n- **37%** better message delivery after consolidating 27+ messaging systems",
  ai="AI in the search platform:\n\n- **Retrieval with citations:** answers grounded in connected sources, with the source shown\n- **Role-aware results:** answers shaped by who is asking\n- **Agents:** a marketplace of verified, ready-made agents\n- **Configurable models:** admins choose the AI model in plain-language settings",
  learnings="Reflections from the project:\n\n- **Trust drives adoption** more than AI performance does\n- **Sources with every answer** make verification easy\n- **Transparency about failures** and pending states builds confidence\n- Enterprise AI must be designed for **admins and compliance reviewers**, not only end users",
  role="Vishnu was the **Lead Product Designer**, owning design end to end from client brief to developer handoff, with ICD as design partner to UnifyApps. The product team defined the roles and led the research. Timeline: 2025 – present, web and mobile.")

ADEO = "https://vishnuprasad.space/work/adeo"
E("adeo", "Committee Board Agentic Application (DGE / ADEO)",
  ["adeo", "dge", "abu dhabi", "committee board", "committee", "board management", "abu dhabi executive office",
   "department of government enablement", "committee platform", "voting platform", "governance app", "board app",
   "committee intelligence", "deliberation", "voting"],
  overview="**Committee Board Agentic Application (DGE / ADEO, Abu Dhabi)**\n\nA government platform that helps the Abu Dhabi Executive Office's committees **analyse, deliberate on, vote on and record decisions** on 1,000+ high-impact proposals a month.\n\n- **Client:** UnifyApps for DGE and ADEO\n- **Partners:** Frog Design and Nagarro Design (ICD as design partner)\n- **Platform:** Tablet-first, plus web\n- **Timeline:** April 2025 – February 2026\n- **Role:** Lead Product Designer" + L(ADEO),
  problem="ADEO handles **1,000+ high-impact submissions every month**, mostly Arabic PDFs and presentations. Preparation could take **up to 15 working days**. Four structural problems:\n\n1. **Slow preparation:** members skimmed documents right before sessions\n2. **Unsearchable history:** five years of decisions (about 3,000–4,000 documents) couldn't be used during deliberation\n3. **Absent members had no voice:** no way to contribute or record a position\n4. **Incomplete records:** minutes, resolutions and action items were scattered",
  users="Three user types:\n\n- **Committee members:** about **15 minutes per topic**, so they need structured briefings\n- **Secretaries:** own the long preparation and documentation around each session\n- **Observers and admins:** need visibility without the ability to act\n\nResearch was continuous: requirements came directly from the client and departments, validated at each major decision.",
  features="The core flow is **Analyse → Deliberate → Decide & Record**:\n\n- **Session agenda:** members see only their committees, active session on top, proposals split into *For Information* and *Decision Making*\n- **AI analysis and briefing:** a summary, strategic alignment score, ROI estimate, feasibility rating and risk assessment for every proposal, shown before the document\n- **AI assistant:** searches the five-year archive from inside the session\n- **Voting and async participation:** five outcomes, each requiring a rationale; absent members can vote and give feedback\n- **Live documentation:** minutes, action items and resolution drafts generated during the session",
  strategy="Vishnu structured the product around how committees actually work: **Analyse → Deliberate → Decide & Record**.\n\n- **Briefing first:** members have ~15 minutes per topic, so the AI briefing appears before the raw document\n- **Scoped arrival:** each member sees only their own committees\n- **Deliberate voting:** every vote needs a rationale\n- **Records as a by-product:** documentation is generated live, so nothing is drafted after the session\n- **Tablet-first:** the proposal stays central and the assistant is collapsed by default",
  decisions="Every decision came with a named cost:\n\n- **Scoping members to their own committees** keeps arrival focused, but multi-committee members need a separate view\n- **AI content first** speeds understanding, but trust has to be earned immediately\n- **Mandatory voting rationale** makes voting deliberately slower; that friction is right for government decisions\n- **Proposal over assistant on tablet:** the assistant is collapsed by default to protect focus",
  outcomes="Impact as reported in the case study:\n\n- **Preparation:** up to 15 working days → **minutes**, via AI-generated briefings\n- **History:** 3,000–4,000 documents across 5 years became **queryable mid-session**\n- **Scale:** **1,000+ proposals a month** analysed, deliberated, voted on and documented in one platform\n- **Documentation:** minutes, action items and resolution drafts generated **live**",
  ai="AI in ADEO:\n\n- **Proposal briefings:** summary, strategic alignment score, ROI estimate, feasibility rating and risk assessment\n- **Archive assistant:** conversational search across five years of decisions\n- **Live documentation:** minutes, action items and resolution drafts generated during the session\n- **Clear labelling:** AI content is always marked, and humans approve before anything becomes an official record",
  learnings="Reflections:\n\n- **Label AI clearly** so people always know what was machine-generated\n- **Important decisions deserve deliberate interactions**, not speed\n- **People stay in control:** AI drafts; humans review, edit and approve before anything becomes official",
  role="Vishnu was the **Lead Product Designer**, working through UnifyApps for DGE and ADEO alongside **Frog Design** and **Nagarro Design**, with ICD as design partner. April 2025 – February 2026, tablet-first with web.",
  voting="Voting is deliberately structured:\n\n- **Five outcomes:** Approve, Approve with Comments, Not Approved, Return for Committee, Abstain\n- **A rationale is required** for every vote, creating a record of why each decision was made\n- **Absent members** can vote asynchronously and give feedback across four dimensions\n\nThe extra friction is intentional: government decisions should be considered, not rushed.")

