  problem="India's DPDP Act set a deadline the bank **couldn't move**.\n\n- Customers needed to **see** what the bank holds, **control** what they agreed to, and **withdraw consent** any time\n- Operations needed every purpose **configured, versioned and auditable**\n- Consent was *collected everywhere and governed nowhere*: scattered across legacy systems, reconciled by hand, hard to act on in real time",
  users="Two sides of one system:\n\n- **Customers:** see, control and withdraw consent\n- **Bank operators and the Data Privacy Office:** configure purposes, version them, monitor violations and audit\n\nBoth sides were designed together on **one shared consent record**.",
